  "dct_description_sm": [
    "Melville Peninsula is situated transitionally between two modern climate regimes and is an important region for archaeology of Thule sites. Thus, the goal of this project is to provide paleoenvironmental records for the periods preceding and during the Thule occupation. Paleoenvironmental indicators were selected to provide information on past temperatures, vegetation, seasonality, lake ice and aquatic ecosystems."
  ],
